From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:00:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): start a new chat in a project from the command
 palette

The palette's "New chat" always opens a plain composer, so starting a
session with a project's stored defaults (host, workspace, agent, model,
worktree) meant leaving the keyboard for the sidebar's per-project pencil.

Typing in the palette now also lists "New chat in <project>" rows, which
open the composer at /?project=<name>, the same route the pencil uses.
Every typed word must appear in the label, so "new omni" and "omni" both
match. The rows stay hidden while the query is empty so a long project
list doesn't push Actions out of view, and the sessions-only switcher
leaves them out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6cc98f0bde341d08c447c2d5b0d324959b163036)
